[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4363754272","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119056#issuecomment-4363754272","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119056","id":4363754272,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBBmbIA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-02T12:13:30Z","updated_at":"2026-05-02T12:13:30Z","body":"Given that this will change a default and break compatibility (ie Pico users will need to enable this setting for their apps to keep working correctly), I think we need to be very sure that we've picked the right default. I wouldn't want to change it, only to realize we should have picked a different default, and then we are potentially faced with breaking compatibility again.\r\n\r\nSo, I'd like to get clarity on what the spec means here before moving forward.\r\n\r\nIf my original interpretation of the spec is correct, then the current PR is good (ie use Vulkan-style Y direction by default). If instead, the spec only intends to define the range of NDC and leave the Y direction unspecified, then I'd probably want to change this PR to use the Y direction of the graphics API by default, and have the Y flip setting invert that, because that will work on more headsets out-of-the-box\r\n\r\nIf we can get clarity on that before Godot 4.7-rc1, then perhaps we can try to get this into 4.7","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4363754272/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4918476921","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119056#issuecomment-4918476921","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119056","id":4918476921,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJSoAeQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-08T19:28:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T19:28:00Z","body":"At this point, I've come around to thinking that the spec isn't clear enough and the expected Y direction of the motion vectors is essentially undefined\r\n\r\nSo, rather than changing our default, I've updated the PR to keep it how it was (which is also compatible with more OpenXR runtimes and devices) and have the setting flip the Y direction from that\r\n\r\nThis means that folks targeting Android XR will need to enable the setting, but it won't need to be used on Meta and Pico. I've updated the example in the docs to reflect this.\r\n\r\nHopefully, we can eventually get an update to the spec (probably in the form of a new version of the extension) which makes this setting unnecessary","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4918476921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4928242988","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119056#issuecomment-4928242988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119056","id":4928242988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJb8FLA","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-09T18:21:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T18:21:31Z","body":"> This means that folks targeting Android XR will need to enable the setting, but it won't need to be used on Meta and Pico. I've updated the example in the docs to reflect this.\n\nCan you update the vendors plugin to show a warning in the export window if this setting is not enabled for Android XR when frame synthesis is on.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4928242988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4959638765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119056#issuecomment-4959638765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119056","id":4959638765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ54U7Q","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T15:28:18Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T15:28:18Z","body":"> Can you update the vendors plugin to show a warning in the export window if this setting is not enabled for Android XR when frame synthesis is on.\r\n\r\nSure! Implemented here: https://github.com/GodotVR/godot_openxr_vendors/pull/508","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4959638765/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4959799225","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119056#issuecomment-4959799225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119056","id":4959799225,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ6CHuQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T15:44:59Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T15:44:59Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/r